From e17f4ba098328e384d924cd5c8e706eec9be20f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lolren <loren.bufanu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 13:04:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] software_isp: render contiguous NV12 in one target

Import a linear NV12 allocation as one GR88 framebuffer and write its
luma and chroma rows in a single filtered draw. Keep the existing
readback/libyuv path as a safe fallback for non-contiguous or unsupported
buffers.

This preserves the five-tap luma sharpness and 2x2 chroma averaging
while avoiding GPU readback and CPU colour conversion on compatible
Waydroid buffers.

Signed-off-by: Lolren <loren.bufanu@gmail.com>
